# CNC Pipeline Layer Sequence — Implementation Plan

## Summary

Add per-NC-program layer sequencing control so users can reorder CNC operation layers
(FREZ, CUT, HOLES, FREZ_135) from both the teleported navbar and the settings dialog,
triggering regeneration with a `custom_sequence` parameter sent to the backend.

**No Convex schema changes required.** The sequence is derived from scenario + detected
layers on the frontend and passed as `custom_sequence` to the backend on each
generate/regenerate call.

---

## Architecture Overview

### Current Flow
```
DXF upload → detect_scenario() → SCENARIOS[scenario] → hardcoded toolpath_sequence → G-code
```

### New Flow
```
DXF upload → detect_scenario() → derive default sequence → user reorders → custom_sequence → G-code
                                  ↑                          ↑
                           frontend state              passed to backend
```

The key insight: each layer has a **fixed tool assignment** (CUT→T7, HOLES→T7, FREZ→T9,
FREZ_135→T11). Reordering is simply reordering the `(layer, tool_num)` pairs. Tool
assignments never change — only execution order does.

